From f1a6ef63a2703a00fb4832411d2a662a5493c289 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Wed, 15 Jul 2026 10:13:40 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07185/11362] [outer-loop] REQ-ARC-FCP-5699-4: early-trigger
 the soft SGE nudge, races hard collapse gate

Fixes the structural gap found in the prior 3-game re-test: the soft
reflect()-prompt nudge (REQ-ARC-FCP-5699-3) was nested entirely
inside the periodic reflect_every=6 schedule, while the hard
AntiStagnationDiversityController collapse gate is checked on EVERY
rank() call -- so on any game whose dynamics trip hard collapse
before the next scheduled boundary, the soft path never got a turn
at all (0/3 games fired it in the prior real-GPU run).

SGECandidateRouter.rank() now checks the same soft signal reflect()
itself uses (consecutive null outcomes / a non-empty taboo set) on
every call in the non-collapsed branch, not just on schedule. When
present early, reflect() fires immediately
(reflection_trigger="early_stagnation_signal") rather than waiting
or losing the race to the hard gate. Purely additive: a healthy run
with no stagnation signal is unaffected (still "scheduled" only).

Real-GPU re-test of the same 3-game suite (prior run preserved as
*_pre_5699_4_early_trigger_baseline.json): the fix works as designed
-- nudge_fired=True on ALL 3 games now (vs 0/3 before), reflect()
firing 4/2/6 times respectively. Parse quality with the wider token
budget: 9/12 successful overall -- cd82 went 0-fires to 6/6 clean,
on-topic advice; sk48 still 0/2 (unexplained, game-specific); g50t
showed a new failure mode (the model meta-commenting on its own
prompt instead of answering). Headline metric unchanged: still 0/3
leveled up, even with cd82's advice landing cleanly and repeatedly --
an honest, now-answerable question the mechanism previously couldn't
even pose. Logged in ops/known-issues.md task 6 with concrete next
steps (sk48 parse-failure investigation, whether cd82's advice is
actually followed by propose(), a longer budget on cd82 specifically
since its mechanism is now demonstrably healthy).

4 new unit tests (early-trigger fires before schedule, scheduled-only
label preserved on healthy runs, no-fire when nothing stagnates).
Spec: REQ-ARC-FCP-5699-4 with its own scenario + spec-declaration
test, matching the sibling REQ-ARC-FCP-5699/5699-2/5699-3 pattern.

